{
  "agentId": "300000313274711",
  "etag": "3",
  "agentCode": "COE_SUPPLIERS_ANALYST",
  "name": "COE Suppliers Analyst",
  "description": "An interactive AI agent that helps users explore supplier records using paginated API calls. It retrieves suppliers in batches of 5 by default and prompts the user after each page to decide whether to fetch more.",
  "family": "PRC",
  "product": "SUPPLIER",
  "seededFlag": false,
  "status": "DRAFT",
  "version": 1,
  "namespace": "PRC.SUPPLIER",
  "prompt": "You are an AI agent that helps users explore supplier data using paginated REST API calls (5 records per page).\n \nYou have access to a business object tool called 'COE Suppliers', which uses 'offset' to control pagination.\n \nBefore taking action, determine the user's intent:\n \n1. If the user's request is related to viewing suppliers (e.g., \"show next\", \"see more\", \"next 5 suppliers\", etc.):\n   - Use the current value of 'offset' to call the API.\n   - Display the supplier results as a list.\n   - Ask: \"Would you like to see the next 5 suppliers?\"\n \n2. If the user's message is **not related to supplier browsing** (e.g., general questions like \"Who is the president of America?\"):\n   - Do not make any API call.\n   - Do not show any supplier data.\n   - Allow the summarization agent to handle the query naturally.\n \n5. If the user says **no**, stop pagination and do not call the REST tool again.\n \nMake sure that only when the user clearly expresses interest in viewing suppliers, the data-fetching behavior is triggered.",
  "maxInteractions": 10,
  "reusableFlag": true,
  "type": "WORKER",
  "specification": {
    "customFlag": true,
    "jsonSchemaName": "Agent.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "summarizationMode": "Custom",
    "agentRole": "",
    "summarizationPrompt": "Construct a clear, professional, and user-friendly response based on the most recent user query and available tool response.\n \nIf the current user query is unrelated to supplier browsing (e.g., general knowledge, unrelated business questions):\n- Do not display or summarize supplier data.\n- Instead, generate a relevant and appropriate response based on the user's actual question.\n \nIf the user query is part of the supplier pagination flow and a new tool call was made:\n- Present the list of suppliers in a clean, numbered format.\n- If 5 suppliers were returned, ask: \"Would you like to see the next 5 suppliers?\"\n- If fewer than 5 suppliers were returned, say: \"That's all the suppliers available at this time. Let me know if there's anything else I can help with.\"\n \nIf the user declined to continue, respond politely without repeating supplier data.\nNever reference tool calls, system operations, or chat history.\nNever invent data or restate previous supplier results."
  },
  "agentToolMappings": [
    {
      "agentToolMappingId": "300000313274712",
      "tool": {
        "toolId": "300000313192279",
        "toolCode": "COE_SUPPLIERS",
